WHAT WAS DERIVED

The upstream project's *design* is the starting point of this work, and the
following are deliberately preserved (each is marked in the source with an
`upstream v2.5.6` comment):

  * the `did = sha256(raw 32-byte Ed25519 public key)[..8]` identity
    construction (this rewrite mints `did:nau:` and also ACCEPTS the upstream
    `did:aip:` prefix, so upstream identities remain verifiable);
  * the canonical-payload semantics: drop `signature`, compact separators,
    lexicographic key order, non-ASCII left raw;
  * the settlement conservation invariant
    `balance_sum = total_deposited - total_slashed` with an O(1) incremental
    check plus an independent O(N) audit;
  * BFT-lite's parameters and rules: `n >= 3f+1`, quorum `2f+1`, whole-round
    voiding on equivocation, `silence > f => NoQuorum`;
  * the six-field task specification (goal / context / done / todo / trace /
    owner) and the three-level evidence grading
    (verified / cpu-proto / unverified, defaulting closed);
  * the Lv1-Lv7 layered-topology concept, the relay classification
    (Dedicated > SelfHosted > ThirdParty > General) and the relay-pool capacity
    formula;
  * actor-owned market state, task-id-keyed settlement idempotency, and the
    deterministic seeded experiment harness.

WHAT WAS NOT COPIED

No upstream source file was copied. The Rust workspace, the Python SDK, the
JavaScript SDK, the Solidity contracts and the CI configuration were written
from scratch against a per-defect audit of upstream. See:

  * ATTRIBUTION.md       - provenance, preservation and replacement tables
  * docs/GAP-ANALYSIS.md - the per-defect audit (76 defects with file:line
                           evidence and quoted upstream source)

The single exception is test *data*: the conformance vector identified as
`upstream-v2.5.6-compat` in conformance/vectors.json reproduces the constants
pinned by upstream's own test `gsn-core/tests/cross_lang_signature.rs`
(public key, DID, canonical payload and signature). It is included precisely to
prove byte-level backward compatibility with upstream identities.

